{"track":"est2l2","num":"5.01","slug":"introductory-calculus","title":"Introductory Calculus","sections":[{"heading":"Section 1: Limits & Continuity","questions":[{"q":"Evaluate $\\lim_{x \\to 2} \\frac{x^3 - 8}{x - 2}$.","choices":["$12$","$8$","$4$","Does not exist"],"correct":0,"answer":"Factor difference of cubes: $\\lim_{x \\to 2} \\frac{(x - 2)(x^2 + 2x + 4)}{x - 2} = \\lim_{x \\to 2} (x^2 + 2x + 4) = 4 + 4 + 4 = 12$."},{"q":"Evaluate $\\lim_{x \\to 0} \\frac{\\tan(3x)}{x}$.","choices":["$3$","$1$","$\\frac{1}{3}$","$0$"],"correct":0,"answer":"$\\lim_{x \\to 0} \\frac{\\sin(3x)}{x \\cos(3x)} = 3 \\lim_{x \\to 0} \\frac{\\sin(3x)}{3x} \\cdot \\frac{1}{\\cos(3x)} = 3(1)(1) = 3$."},{"q":"What value of $a$ makes $f(x) = \\frac{x^2 - 1}{x - 1}$ for $x \\neq 1$, and $f(1) = a$ continuous at $x = 1$?","choices":["$2$","$1$","$0$","$-1$"],"correct":0,"answer":"$\\lim_{x \\to 1} \\frac{(x - 1)(x + 1)}{x - 1} = \\lim_{x \\to 1} (x + 1) = 2$. For continuity, $f(1) = a = 2$."}]},{"heading":"Section 2: Derivatives & Power/Product Rules","questions":[{"q":"Find the derivative of $f(x) = 4x^3 - 5x^2 + 7x - 9$.","choices":["$12x^2 - 10x + 7$","$12x^2 - 5x + 7$","$4x^2 - 10x + 7$","$12x^3 - 10x^2 + 7$"],"correct":0,"answer":"By power rule: $\\frac{d}{dx}(4x^3) = 12x^2$, $\\frac{d}{dx}(-5x^2) = -10x$, $\\frac{d}{dx}(7x) = 7$."},{"q":"What is the slope of the tangent line to $y = x^2 e^x$ at $x = 1$?","choices":["$3e$","$2e$","$e$","$4e$"],"correct":0,"answer":"Product rule: $y' = 2x e^x + x^2 e^x = e^x(2x + x^2)$. At $x = 1$: $y'(1) = e^1(2 + 1) = 3e$."},{"q":"What is the derivative of $g(x) = \\frac{2x + 1}{x - 3}$?","choices":["$-\\frac{7}{(x - 3)^2}$","$\\frac{7}{(x - 3)^2}$","$\\frac{2}{(x - 3)^2}$","$-\\frac{5}{(x - 3)^2}$"],"correct":0,"answer":"Quotient rule: $\\frac{2(x - 3) - (2x + 1)(1)}{(x - 3)^2} = \\frac{2x - 6 - 2x - 1}{(x - 3)^2} = -\\frac{7}{(x - 3)^2}$."}]},{"heading":"Section 3: Chain Rule & Extrema","questions":[{"q":"Find the derivative of $h(x) = (3x^2 - 5)^4$.","choices":["$24x(3x^2 - 5)^3$","$4(3x^2 - 5)^3$","$12x(3x^2 - 5)^3$","$24(3x^2 - 5)^3$"],"correct":0,"answer":"Chain rule: $4(3x^2 - 5)^3 \\cdot \\frac{d}{dx}(3x^2 - 5) = 4(3x^2 - 5)^3 (6x) = 24x(3x^2 - 5)^3$."},{"q":"At what value of $x$ does $f(x) = 2x^3 - 9x^2 + 12x + 1$ have a local minimum?","choices":["$x = 2$","$x = 1$","$x = 0$","$x = 3$"],"correct":0,"answer":"$f'(x) = 6x^2 - 18x + 12 = 6(x^2 - 3x + 2) = 6(x - 1)(x - 2) = 0$. $f''(x) = 12x - 18$. At $x = 2$: $f''(2) = 6 > 0$ (local min)."},{"q":"What is the acceleration of a particle at $t = 2$ if its position is $s(t) = t^3 - 6t^2 + 5t$?","choices":["$0$","$5$","$-7$","$6$"],"correct":0,"answer":"Velocity $v(t) = s'(t) = 3t^2 - 12t + 5$. Acceleration $a(t) = v'(t) = 6t - 12$. At $t = 2$: $a(2) = 6(2) - 12 = 0$."}]},{"heading":"Section 4: Definite Integrals & Fundamental Theorem","questions":[{"q":"Evaluate the definite integral: $\\int_0^3 (3x^2 - 2x + 1) dx$.","choices":["$21$","$18$","$24$","$27$"],"correct":0,"answer":"Antiderivative is $[x^3 - x^2 + x]_0^3 = (27 - 9 + 3) - 0 = 21$."},{"q":"What is the area of the region bounded by $y = 4 - x^2$ and the $x$-axis?","choices":["$\\frac{32}{3}$","$\\frac{16}{3}$","$16$","$8$"],"correct":0,"answer":"Roots are $x = \\pm 2$: $\\int_{-2}^2 (4 - x^2) dx = 2 \\int_0^2 (4 - x^2) dx = 2 [4x - \\frac{x^3}{3}]_0^2 = 2 [8 - \\frac{8}{3}] = 2 [\\frac{16}{3}] = \\frac{32}{3}$."},{"q":"If $\\int_1^4 f(x) dx = 7$, what is $\\int_1^4 [2f(x) + 3] dx$?","choices":["$23$","$17$","$20$","$26$"],"correct":0,"answer":"$2 \\int_1^4 f(x) dx + \\int_1^4 3 dx = 2(7) + 3(4 - 1) = 14 + 9 = 23$."}]}]}